media: iris: gen1 encoder controls and input layout for Sunshine

Korri-local, on top of media-iris-sm8150-legacy-vpu5.patch. Sunshine's
h264_v4l2m2m path needs all three. The Retroid Pocket Mini V2 carries the same
changes for SM8250 against upstream Iris (nix/devices/rpminiv2/kernel:
product-patches/9999-media-qcom-iris-add-request-key-frame-support.patch,
product-patches/9999-media-qcom-iris-gen1-repeat-headers.patch and
patches/9999-media-qcom-iris-gen1-visible-encoder-resolution.patch); these
are their ports to the nabu Iris tree, gen1 only.

- V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_FORCE_KEY_FRAME maps to the dynamic
  HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_REQUEST_SYNC_FRAME (0x2006004). It has no payload,
  but the packet size still counts the property id; without it the firmware
  fails the session with HFI_ERR_SESSION_CMDSIZE (0x100e).
- V4L2_CID_MPEG_VIDEO_PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR is exposed; when set, the gen1
  HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_SYNC_FRAME_SEQUENCE_HEADER boolean is on even with
  HEADER_MODE_SEPARATE.
- The OUTPUT (raw) format reports the aligned storage size (width to 128,
  height to 32), as upstream Iris does. The firmware reads the chroma plane
  after the aligned height (UNCOMPRESSED_PLANE_ACTUAL_INFO); the port reported
  the visible height, so clients wrote chroma 16 rows early at 1280x720 and
  the picture's colours were shifted. The visible size is the crop: it is the
  firmware's input frame size and the bitstream size.

